# ============================================================
#  Clues and leads (playtest 2, X11) as the Journal shows them.
#  kind: clue is one of its arc's clues: and counts in clues(arc);
#  kind: lead points somewhere to look, never counts, and is
#  struck through once its followed: holds. Only hard-canon story
#  cards find clues; a lead may come from any story beat.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- The Hollow Star: leads ----------------

@clue lead_lake_breathed
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: The lake held its breath
text: In Mistveil the lake froze for one breath and the drowned bell tolled. Whoever keeps the boathouse has heard that shore for years.
followed: clue(lake_bell)

@clue lead_founders_archive
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: What the founders wrote
text: The headmistress told the hall it was nothing. The founders' records in the library archive may disagree, and the Restricted Section keeps what the archive won't.
followed: clue(founders_ledger)

@clue lead_maud_friend
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: Maud lost a friend
text: Old Maud was a student the last time the lake froze, and lost a friend to it. She might tell you more, if she trusts you.
followed: clue(knows_founders_seal)

@clue lead_man_in_grey
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: A man in grey
text: A man in a grey coat told Kael to open something, or his sister would. Kael knows what. He'll tell someone he trusts.
followed: clue(kael_family)

@clue lead_black_star_dream
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: A dream of a black star
text: You dreamt of the lake from underneath. Seraphine dreams too, and the observatory sees further than any dream.
followed: clue(second_shadow)

@clue lead_seventh_tower
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: The seventh tower
text: Seven towers, seven locks. One tower has been locked for a century, and something is kept at the top of it.
followed: clue(star_key)

@clue lead_white_furs
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: A girl in white furs
text: A Northern girl has taken a room above the village bakery. Kael went pale when he heard.
followed: met(ilse)

@clue heard_of_starcalling
arc: hollowstar
kind: lead
name: A scraped-out word
text: One word has been scraped out of the observatory's oldest logs. Students who finished Advanced Astromancy were taught it aloud.
followed: enrolled(starcalling) or passed(starcalling, 1)

# ---------------- The Hollow Star: clues ----------------

@clue founders_ledger
arc: hollowstar
name: The razored page
text: The founding year was cut out of the Founders' Ledger with a razor, but the pen's impression survived on the page beneath.

@clue knows_founders_seal
arc: hollowstar
name: The founders' seal
text: Lumenhold was built as a seal: seven towers, seven locks, and a key shaped like a star. Something sleeps beneath the water.

@clue lake_bell
arc: hollowstar
name: The bell under the water
text: A drowned bell lies under the lake and tolls when the thing below stirs. A tunnel runs down from the boathouse toward it.

@clue second_shadow
arc: hollowstar
name: A second shadow
text: Something small and dark crossed the sky the wrong way and stopped directly above the lake.

@clue seven_locks
arc: hollowstar
name: Seven locks
text: One lock in each tower; when a tower goes dark, so does its lock. Locks can be mended. They need hands, and a key.

@clue star_key
arc: hollowstar
name: The star key
text: A key shaped like a star that holds no light, kept at the top of the seventh tower. The seal can't be renewed without it, or without the founders' words.

@clue kael_family
arc: hollowstar
name: The Dumonts
text: Kael's family serve the thing under the lake. They sent him to open its door. He came to stop them.

@clue ilse_truth
arc: hollowstar
name: What Ilse was raised for
text: The Dumonts raised Kael's sister to open the door if he wouldn't. Nobody ever asked her if she wanted to.

@clue codex_names
arc: hollowstar
name: The Codex of Hollow Names
text: A book in the Restricted Section lists everyone the Star has noticed. The last name is still being written, and it is yours.

# ---------------- The Bell Under the Water ----------------

@clue bell_heard
arc: the_bell
name: A bell where none is
text: The drowned bell rang in the night with no one near it, and nobody else woke.

@clue bell_rope
arc: the_bell
name: The cut rope
text: Maud has kept the bell's rope for sixty years. It came up the night the lake froze, cut clean.

@clue bell_name
arc: the_bell
name: The name on the rim
text: Letters run around the bell's rim on the lakebed: a name you don't know, and now keep.

@clue lead_maud_answer
arc: the_bell
kind: lead
name: What Maud knows
text: Maud has kept the bell's rope for sixty years, and she has promised to tell you who cut it. Go and see her at her cottage.
followed: seen(bell_answer) > 0

@clue lead_bell_dive
arc: the_bell
kind: lead
name: The diving helmet
text: There's an old diving helmet in the boathouse. Whatever is written on the bell, you'll only read it from the lakebed.
followed: clue(bell_name)

@clue lead_bell_shore
arc: the_bell
kind: lead
name: The lakeshore after dark
text: The bell wants you at the lakeshore after dark, in the evening or at midnight, with what you have: the name from its rim, or Maud's rope.
followed: flag(bell_silenced)

# ---------------- Second Place ----------------

@clue black_seal_letters
arc: lyra_and_her_mother
name: Letters under a black seal
text: House Vaneshade writes to Lyra under its black seal. Her mother asks who beat her, never how she is.

# ---------------- Side threads (feedback 2026-10-15): hinted now, to be followed up later ----------------
# A side thread's lead names no arc; the Clues panel groups it under its thread:. They never touch the mystery.

@clue lead_moonpetal
thread: The cold that won't leave
kind: lead
name: Moonpetal
text: Old Maud says the cure is a moonpetal from the Whisperwood, which blooms only after dark, and that you have to fetch it yourself.
followed: not has(umbral_curse)

@clue lead_second_timetable
thread: The unsigned note
kind: lead
name: A second timetable
text: Someone slipped a note under your door: the castle has a second timetable, and it starts at midnight. Whoever wrote it knows the passages.
followed: seen(corvin_note_was_mine) > 0

@clue lead_grisk_jetty
thread: Grisk's parcels
kind: lead
name: The jetty at midnight
text: Grisk's arrangement: a parcel collected at the boathouse jetty at midnight, carried to a cobbler's back door in the village by day.
followed: seen(grisk_pickup) > 0 or flag(grisk_gone)

@clue lead_grisk_bottles
thread: Grisk's bottles
kind: lead
name: Bottles at the jetty
text: Grisk's arrangement: a bottle of Brightwater or Owl's Ink for a favour, at the boathouse jetty at midnight.
followed: seen(grisk_elixir_favour) > 0 or flag(grisk_gone) or not flag(grisk_supply)

@clue lead_silver_key
thread: The silver key
kind: lead
name: The Restricted Section
text: Odile Varn's notebook came with a silver key to the Restricted Section, the locked door at the back of the library. It's yours to use after hours, in the evening or at midnight.
followed: seen(forbidden_section_1) > 0 or flag(forbidden_abandoned)

@clue lead_restricted_shelves
thread: The silver key
kind: lead
name: Deeper in the stacks
text: You've been inside the Restricted Section once, and there are shelves you didn't reach. The key still works after hours.
followed: flag(forbidden_read) or seen(forbidden_section_3) > 0

@clue lead_codex_open
thread: The silver key
kind: lead
name: The Codex, left open
text: The Codex of Hollow Names is still lying where it fell in the Restricted Section, open at your name. Sooner or later, someone will notice you've been there.
followed: seen(forbidden_section_3) > 0

@clue lead_newt_upstairs
thread: The upstairs room
kind: lead
name: A regular at the Newt
text: The landlady of the Gilded Newt's upstairs room keeps a jacket for you now. Any night out at the Newt, there's a party upstairs that pays.
followed: seen(newt_company_regular) > 0

@clue lead_sky_championship
thread: The Skyrace team
kind: lead
name: The championship
text: You made the team. The championship against Thornwick is flown at the flight field later in the year.
followed: seen(sky_championship) > 0

# Spells v2 club and job chains (docs/spells-v2-list.md §G; content/events/club_spell_chains.grim): each start card
# leaves a lead, followed once the spell is learned.

@clue lead_brace
thread: The captain's charm
kind: lead
name: The dummy that hexes back
text: An old duelling captain's charm is sewn into the practice dummy, and it throws hexes back. Read the captain's notes, stand Bram's barrage, drill your footwork: then hold firm inside the circle while it empties.
followed: spell_level(brace) >= 1

@clue lead_quickquill
thread: The quill that talks back
kind: lead
name: A quill of your own
text: A spare quill from the Ledger's drying line finishes your sentences, and then invents them. Teach it, give it proper ink and sit a deadline night with it, before the interview where everyone denies everything.
followed: spell_level(quickquill) >= 1

@clue lead_bramble
thread: The seed in your pocket
kind: lead
name: A seed that answers back
text: A seed from the Verdant Circle's far bed sprouted in your pocket. Plant it, see it through a cold snap, and quiet the mandrakes around it before the night it bolts.
followed: spell_level(bramble) >= 1

@clue lead_index
thread: Footnote's drawer
kind: lead
name: The drawer Footnote guards
text: Footnote sits on one catalogue drawer in the library and won't move. Under him is the card for a book eleven years overdue, somewhere on shelves that wander.
followed: spell_level(index) >= 1

@clue lead_rapport
thread: Two taps on the bar
kind: lead
name: How the landlady does it
text: The Newt's landlady taps the bar twice and a fight turns into a laugh. Learn the regulars' stories, stand them a round and work a double shift, and one festival night the room will be yours to hold.
followed: spell_level(rapport) >= 1

@clue lead_distil
thread: Pell's oldest drawer
kind: lead
name: A draught of your own strength
text: Pell's oldest drawer holds a recipe for a draught "of your own strength". Count drops with Pell, buy moonwort, try the daughters' shortcut, and then brew it.
followed: spell_level(purify) >= 1

@clue lead_tailwind
thread: The jar of wind
kind: lead
name: Wind in a jar
text: A jar of wind sits on the courier loft's dead-letter shelf, and someone once flew with it. Find out who, race the gulls and fix the broom that pulls left, then fly a storm delivery across the lake.
followed: spell_level(tailwind) >= 1

# World expansion 1: the Whisperwood delve

@clue lead_the_hush
thread: The Hush
kind: lead
name: The Hush
text: The deepest part of the Whisperwood, past the heartwood, keeps the castle's hours: it wakes only at midnight.
followed: flag(ww_hush_seen)

@clue lead_heartwood
thread: The elder oak's gift
kind: lead
name: A splinter of heartwood
text: The elder oak gave you a splinter of its heartwood. Mir, at the market stall, could carve it into a wand.
followed: has_item(heartwood_wand)

@clue lead_spinner_silk
thread: The Spinner's silk
kind: lead
name: A bolt of grey silk
text: The Spinner gave you a bolt of her silk. The village tailor could make a robe of it.
followed: has_item(spinner_silk_robe)

@clue lead_missed_round
thread: The missed round
kind: lead
name: The lamp that went out
text: Sister Amaranth missed her evening round, the first time anyone can remember. Someone has to keep the infirmary going until she's on her feet, in the evenings, bed by bed.
followed: flag(rounds_finished)

@clue lead_red_ink
thread: Red ink
kind: lead
name: Two sets of marks
text: Someone is marking your essays a second time, in red ink and unsigned, and leaving them on the lecture tower stair. They expect the next draft there too.
followed: flag(red_ink_finished)

@clue lead_late_bloomer
thread: The sweet shop's daughter
kind: lead
name: The cold stove
text: The sweet shop owner's grown daughter boils the sugar on a cold stove when she's upset, and nobody at home knows what to do about it. You're the one from the castle, and she'll be waiting when you're next home.
followed: flag(bloomer_finished)
